# Claude Code Agent Rules for Sil-More

## CRITICAL: Read This First
Before starting ANY work on this codebase, read `agents.md` in the repo root.

## Active Plan
If there's an active plan file in `.claude/plans/`, check with the user if you should continue from it.
Current active plan: `artefact-enhancements.md` (artefact uniqueness & monster stat reduction)
- Phase 2 ✅ COMPLETE: Monster stat reduction flags (ARMOR_SHATTER, WILL_DRAIN) implemented
- Phase 3 PENDING: Add flags to specific artefacts in lib/edit/artefact.txt

## Key Guidelines from agents.md:
- **Build**: ALWAYS use `.\build-cmake.bat` (never ad-hoc gcc/make/MinGW commands)
- **Incremental rebuild**: `cmake --build build-standard --parallel`
- **New .c files**: Must start with `#include "angband.h"` and be added to CMakeLists.txt
- **Data files**: Templates in `lib/edit/*.txt` compile to `ANGBAND_DIR_DATA`
- **Documentation**: Maximum one working notes file per session: `session_notes.md`

## Quick Reference:
- Core game loop: `src/dungeon.c`, `src/generate.c`, `src/cave.c`
- Player commands: `src/cmd1.c` through `src/cmd6.c`
- Combat/monsters: `src/monster*.c`, `src/melee*.c`, `src/spells*.c`
- Objects: `src/object*.c`, `src/obj-info.c`
- Data templates: `lib/edit/*.txt` (monsters, vaults, objects, artefacts, etc.)

Read the full `agents.md` for complete guidance on build workflow, data management, coding patterns, and subsystem architecture.
